*.sw?

# Windows reserved device names. A file literally called `nul` can be created by
# a shell redirect on Windows and then breaks `git add` with "mmap failed".
nul
NUL
[Cc][Oo][Nn]
[Pp][Rr][Nn]
[Aa][Uu][Xx]

# Build artifact: regenerated by `npm run sitemap` on every build, and never
# served in production (nginx proxies /sitemap.xml to the backend, which builds
# it dynamically so new blog posts appear without a rebuild). Committing it
# guaranteed a merge conflict on every deploy.
public/sitemap.xml
